(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text"
A **Description_text** is a set of words that describe something.
*)

(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text.__example"
The same thing may have multiple descriptions associated with it. Relating both a short description and a long description to an operational activity or an organization, as required by the US DoD Architecture Framework, are examples of multiple descriptions applied to the same item.
*)

(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text.description"
the text that constitutes the description
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment"
A **Description_text_assignment** is the assignment of a description to something.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment.description"
the text that constitutes the description
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment.items"
the set of items being described
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship"
A **Description_text_assignment_relationship** is a relationship between two <<express:Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment,Description_text_assignment>> objects.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.description"
the text or the set of texts that provide further information about the **Description_text_assignment_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.id"
the identifier or set of identifiers for the **Description_text_assignment_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.related"
the other object of <<express:Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment,Description_text_assignment>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.relating"
one object of <<express:Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment,Description_text_assignment>> that is part of the relationship.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.relation_type"
the meaning of the relationship.
*)


(*"Description_assignment_arm.Description_text_assignment_relationship.wr:WR1"
the **related** and the **relating** must be different.
*)


